  "preamble": "Spirantization of the voiced uvular stop /ɢ/ to the voiced uvular fricative or approximant [ʁ]. In standard Iranian (Tehrani) Persian, the merged reflex of Classical Persian ق /q/ and غ /ɣ/ is usually the stop [ɢ], but between vowels in unstressed position it is commonly realized as [ʁ] (or velar [ɣ]); acoustic measurements of Tehrani speakers confirm [ʁ] as a regular free variant of the stop. Dari and Tajik keep /q/ and /ɣ/ apart, so the same words show [q] there.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Spirantization, Lenition",
